{"id":"overtime-in-exempt-classes","tier":"REDFLAG","title":"Overtime paid in classes the manual marks overtime-exempt","question":"How much overtime went in fiscal 2026 to job classes the Compensation Manual lists as exempt (salaried) from overtime?","finding":"20 classes marked exempt were paid $50,000 or more of overtime in fiscal 2026, $5.9 million in all; largest: Protective Services Worker (job 2940, Human Services Agency) $1.5 million to 194 people; Captain 3 (job Q082, Police) $779,710 to 36 people; Protective Services Supervisor (job 2944, Human Services Agency) $767,953 to 44 people. By unit: SEIU, Local 1021, Misc (unit 535) $2.3 million; SEIU, Local 1021, Misc (unit 790) $1.0 million; POA (unit 911) $779,710.","how":"The overtime column (Z exempt, N non-exempt, L comp-time cap) is read from the rate tables of the FY2025-26 Compensation Manual (1,162 job codes parsed, FY2026-27 for codes missing there). Overtime is the Controller's fiscal 2026 rows for each job code.","limits":"'Exempt' is the Fair Labor Standards Act status; labor agreements can still pay exempt staff for extra hours (for example premium or callback pay, or overtime at a straight rate for emergencies), and uniformed managers may be paid overtime by their agreement. The status is the latest manual's; a class can have changed. The text was read from the PDF and a misaligned column could misread a flag.","columns":[{"k":"job","t":"Class","type":"text"},{"k":"jobCode","t":"Job code","type":"text"},{"k":"unit","t":"Union (bargaining unit)","type":"text"},{"k":"department","t":"Main department","type":"text"},{"k":"people","t":"People","type":"int"},{"k":"overtime","t":"Overtime","type":"usd"},{"k":"perPerson","t":"Per person","type":"usd"},{"k":"otShare","t":"Overtime / regular pay","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"job":"Protective Services Worker","jobCode":"2940","unit":"SEIU, Local 1021, Misc (unit 535)","people":194,"overtime":1485750,"perPerson":7659,"otShare":0.0632,"department":"Human Services